    "## 10. Correlation Analysis\n",
    "We compute the correlation coefficients between default status and the key numeric variables to quantify the strength and direction of each relationship. This complements the visual patterns observed in the boxplots above.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Finding**: Interest rate shows the strongest correlation with default (+0.22), followed by FICO score (-0.14). State GDP shows almost no correlation with default (-0.02), confirming the earlier boxplot observation. Notably, FICO and interest rate are strongly negatively correlated (-0.72), indicating that LendingClub's pricing already incorporates credit risk—borrowers with lower FICO scores are charged higher rates."
   ]
