    "## 11. Logistic Regression Analysis\n",
    "We fit a logistic regression model to estimate the effect of each variable on the probability of default, controlling for the other variables simultaneously. Unlike the correlation analysis above, this allows us to assess the independent contribution of each factor.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Findings**:\n",
    "\n",
    "The logistic regression results show that, after controlling for other variables:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Interest rate** has the strongest and most significant positive effect on default probability (coef = 0.155, p < 0.001), consistent with the correlation analysis.\n",
    "- **DTI** is positively and significantly associated with default (coef = 0.014, p = 0.001), confirming that higher debt burden increases default risk.\n",
